The only *chaotic* option.  I thought sacrafice gifts build a
list of the available artifacts by merging your alignment plus
the neutral list, removing the ones that already exist, and
chosing randomly among that list.

What naming Orcrist does is 1) increase the chances of getting
one of the neutral artifacts (probably a good thing) and 2)
decrease the chances of getting second and subsequent gifts
(probably a bad thing).  As usual with Nethack, there is no
clear right answer and it is easy to justify either option.

For a non-wizard elf, Orcrist is in the same skill class as
Stormbringer.  As long as that class starts out unrestricted in
the broadsword category, naming Orcrist is probably a good idea
to get a head start on enhancing the broadsword class.  So I
would look at the list of available weapons skill classes
before deciding.  For a Wizard it's a slam-dunk no based on
a Wizard wanting to spend most skill slots on spell schools.

